				)
			)
		)
		(property "Sourcing_Note" "Replaces the Si1308EDL, which had a 55-week factory lead and a single reel in Digi-Key stock. Chosen for gate drive rather than current: Vgs(th) 1.1 V max with Rds(on) specified down to 2.5 V of gate drive (80 mOhm), so it is fully enhanced from the driver IC's 3.3 V GDR output. Its gate is a heavier load than the Si1308EDL's - Qg 2.9 nC against 1.4 nC typ, Ciss 270 pF against 105 pF, both at 4.5 V - but it matches the Si1304BDL that the panel datasheet's reference circuit offers as its own alternative (Qg 2.7 nC at 4.5 V), so it is within what the GDR output is expected to drive. Peak switch current is set by the 3 ohm sense resistor on RESE and is far below this part's rating, so the current rating is not the binding constraint. ~105,000 in stock, 20-week lead. Qualified second source: Toshiba SSM3K376R, a lighter gate still (Qg 2.2 nC, Ciss 200 pF), but it is SOT-23F flat-lead and would want its own land pattern."
			(at 0 0 180)
			(unlocked yes)
			(layer "F.Fab")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "374c07a4-81a5-41ea-bf5b-09facb0a3351")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1 1)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
			)
		)
