		(property "Sourcing_Note" "Input capacitor on the +3.3V rail feeding the boost inductor - the C4 position in the panel reference circuit. 50V X7R is far beyond what a 3.3V rail needs; the part is shared with the charge-pump flying capacitor to keep a single 4.7uF line item across the project. The side benefit is real though: DC-bias derating is negligible at 3.3V on a 50V part, so the boost input sees close to the full 4.7uF the reference circuit intends, where a 10V 0402 delivered roughly half."
			(at 0 0 270)
			(unlocked yes)
			(layer "F.Fab")
			(hide yes)
